<title>USA: Lockheed unit settles over $4.35 mln backpay.</title>
<headline>Lockheed unit settles over $4.35 mln backpay.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lockheed Martin Corp unit Lockheed Martin Energy Systems Inc has paid $4.35 million in back-pay for employees to settle litigation dating back to a 1991-1992 strike at former Martin Marietta Energy Systems Inc, the National Labor Relations Board said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The money, covering back-pay and interest, will be distributed to about 1,000 employees entitled to compensation under a Board order, the NLRB said in a statement.</p>
<p>The litigation started in 1992 when Local 3-689 of the Oil, Chemical and Atomic Workers International Union filed charges.</p>
